The logic in the 3 ```MemDeltaGens``` functions are in accordance with the 3 different ```UpdatePartialResult``` functions for ```firstValue```, ```lastValue``` and ```nthValue```
From the code in executor/aggfuncs/func_value.go, the 3 ```UpdatePartialResult``` functions are compared as follow:
```
//first: if rowsInGroup is not empty for the first time, memDelta is not zero(for string and json).
p := (*partialResult4FirstValue)(pr)
if p.gotFirstValue {
	return 0, nil
}
if len(rowsInGroup) > 0 {
	p.gotFirstValue = true
	memDelta, err = p.evaluator.evaluateRow(sctx, v.args[0], rowsInGroup[0])
	if err != nil {
		return 0, 
}
return memDelta, nil
```
```
//last: if rowsInGroup is not empty, memDelta is always not zero(for string and json).
p := (*partialResult4LastValue)(pr)
if len(rowsInGroup) > 0 {
	p.gotLastValue = true
	memDelta, err = p.evaluator.evaluateRow(sctx, v.args[0], rowsInGroup[len(rowsInGroup)-1])
	if err != nil {
		return 0, err
	}
}
return memDelta, nil
```
```
//nth: if p.seenRows(which is accumulated rowsInGroups) reached v.nth for the first time, 
//memDelta is not zero(for string and json). Otherwise it is zero.
if v.nth == 0 {
	return 0, nil
}
p := (*partialResult4NthValue)(pr)
numRows := uint64(len(rowsInGroup))
if v.nth > p.seenRows && v.nth-p.seenRows <= numRows {
	memDelta, err = p.evaluator.evaluateRow(sctx, v.args[0], rowsInGroup[v.nth-p.seenRows-1])
	if err != nil {
		return 0, err
	}
}
p.seenRows += numRows
return memDelta, nil
```
So for unit tests consisting 3 rows of type string, their corresponding memDelta should be like:
```
first:     1, 0, 0
1st(nth):  1, 0, 0
2nd(nth):  0, 1, 0
3rd(nth):  0, 0, 1
last:      1, 1, 1
```
The key point here is, for this 3-rows example, first = 1st(nth), but last ≠ 3rd(nth).
Above is what I understood from the original code. If I was wrong, please let me know. Thanks!
